tion/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-110437/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "41954d0a-b8ce-52a0-a2c0-002b0078a37d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-110437"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-43511"] :question/problem "Find the product ${E}_{1}^{-1}{E}_{2}$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{E}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that ${E}_{1}$ and ${E}_{2}$ are both elementary matrices.\n\nFirst, we need to find ${E}_{1}^{-1}.$ We write down ${E}_{1}$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[{E}_{1}\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{E}_{1}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we can find the product ${E}_{1}^{-1}{E}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n{E}_{1}^{-1}{E}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-75239/selection/445a1ac491fc07d8a18d4db303e9cca64570106f878b702c07b6b37e63dd5db1" :answer/id #uuid "ab11438b-0014-5b40-be31-a68d91c8fa5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 23 \\\\ 9 & 0 & -1\\end{align